"id":9521253417049,
"title":"Colombia Honey Aponte",
"handle":"colombia-honey-aponte",
"body_html":"<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><em>From the high-altitude mountains of Aponte, Nariño, Colombia, this exceptional Honey-Processed coffee is produced by smallholder indigenous growers working at elevations between 1,700 and 2,100 meters.</em></p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><em>The Honey process brings together the clarity of a washed coffee with the sweetness and fruit character often associated with natural processing. In the cup, expect a bright and juicy profile with notes of <strong>grapefruit, guava, stone fruit, and caramel</strong>, followed by a smooth sweetness and balanced finish.</em></p>\n<p><em>This is a beautiful representation of specialty coffee from Nariño high grown, vibrant, sweet, and complex, with a distinctive fruit-forward character that makes it a great choice for anyone looking to explore something beyond a traditional Colombian profile`</em></p>\n<p><em>Some of our crew in Captain's Coffee that cupped the Aponte Honey lot reported profiles including <strong data-start=\"1547\" data-end=\"1649\">apricot, peach, marzipan, floral notes, red apple, blood orange, treacle, and honey-like sweetness</strong>.</em></p>",
"published_at":"2026-09-29T09:42:18-04:00",
"created_at":"2026-09-29T07:23:34-04:00",
