"id":9514894131289,
"title":"Jairo Arcila Santa Monica Honey Pink Bourbon (Tartaric Acid / Cinnamon)",
"handle":"jairo-arcila-santa-monica-honey-pink-bourbon-tartaric-acid-cinnamon",
"body_html":"<p dir=\"auto\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\"><em>The ripe Pink Bourbon cherries undergo a <strong>dry anaerobic fermentation</strong>. During the fermentation, <strong>tartaric acid and organic cinnamon are introduced into the fermentation environment</strong>. Documented versions of this coffee report either <strong>48 or 72 hours</strong>, depending on the specific lot. After fermentation, the cherries are pulped and the coffee is dried slowly on raised beds. <span class=\"contents\"><span class=\"\"></span></span><span class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchor\"></span></em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>The <strong>honey process does NOT mean honey is added</strong>. It refers to leaving some of the sticky mucilage on the seed after pulping while the coffee dries.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Tartaric acid is naturally associated with grapes and wine. In controlled coffee fermentation, it can help push the cup toward <strong>brighter fruit, wine-like acidity and greater aromatic definition</strong>.</em></p>\n<p><em><strong>Very limited. Very special. Don’t wait too long!</strong> </em></p>\n<p> </p>",
"published_at":"2026-09-24T10:09:18-04:00",
"created_at":"2026-09-24T05:40:11-04:00",
"updated_at":"2026-11-02T14:43:50-05:00",
